### What changed and why

#### `api/codx/junior/sio/sio.py`

| Change | Detail |
|---|---|
| `io_chat_cancel` payload | Now accepts **both** `chat_id` and `token_id` keys — either alone is sufficient, both may be supplied |
| Fallback logic | `chat_id` is tried first via `CANCELLATION_REGISTRY.cancel`; if that misses (token already unregistered or wrong id), `token_id` is tried via `CANCELLATION_REGISTRY.cancel_by_token_id` |
| Return `method` field | Response now includes `"method": "chat_id"` or `"method": "token_id"` so the client knows which key succeeded |
| Guard for missing both keys | Returns `{ "cancelled": False, "error": "missing chat_id or token_id" }` when neither key is present |
| Logging | Each branch logs at `INFO` on success and `WARNING` on miss, including both keys in the final warning for easy tracing |

