### What changed and why

#### `api/codx/junior/api/chat_cancel_api.py` *(new file)*

| Change | Detail |
|---|---|
| New REST endpoint | `POST /api/chat/cancel` replaces the removed `codx-junior-chat-cancel` Socket.IO event |
| Same dual-key logic | Accepts `chat_id` and/or `token_id`; tries `chat_id` first then falls back to `token_id` |
| Same return shape | `{ "cancelled": bool, "method": "chat_id"|"token_id" }` on success; `{ "cancelled": false, "error": "..." }` on miss |
| No `sid` parameter | REST handler has no socket session concept — logging drops `sid` references accordingly |

#### `api/codx/junior/sio/sio.py`

| Change | Detail |
|---|---|
| `codx-junior-chat-cancel` handler removed | Cancellation is now handled by the REST endpoint; the SIO event is no longer registered |
| `CANCELLATION_REGISTRY` import removed | No longer needed in this module since cancellation logic moved to `chat_cancel_api.py` |
